   :proof
   ["The guard rejects only None. Twelve synthetic malformed values across _SOURCE_IDENTITY and _LAUNCH_IDENTITY, including {}, False, empty strings, invalid digest/length fields and wrong binding labels, reached an explicitly fake Core sentinel instead of being rejected before native work."
    "Separate fully fake initializations completed and published source={} (844-byte record), source=False (879 bytes), and source={sha256: not-a-hash, bytes: -1, binding: wrong} with zero/boolean process clock fields (964 bytes). _warm was a mock throughout."
    "An extra synthetic 65536-character source field was copied into a 66538-byte startup record. Extra synthetic source/path-like and launch/environment-like keys were published verbatim: source is serialized wholesale and process uses dict(_LAUNCH_IDENTITY, pid=...). No real paths, environment values or private data were used in these witnesses."
    "The existing successful-initialization test deliberately supplies source-hash rather than a SHA256 and omits the source binding marker and most process fields, so the six green tests do not establish the requested invalid-binding/schema contract."]
   :impact "Malformed or accidentally corrupted preseeded startup globals can trigger model initialization/warm before failing, or produce an apparently ready but invalid/unbounded identity record. This is a trusted-startup boundary defect, not an HTTP injection exploit: the fixed launcher currently generates valid records and exposes no request-controlled source selection."
   :required-change "Before ov.Core(), reject malformed source/process binding records using a small closed schema: exact permitted keys; 64 lowercase hexadecimal SHA256; positive non-boolean bounded source byte count; exact sha256-of-compile-exec-buffer marker; positive non-boolean bounded start ticks and clock frequency; bounded valid UTC launch timestamp. Serialize only the permitted fields. Keep the pinned launcher as the execution trust base; shape validation is not proof against a forged but validly shaped record."
   :required-regressions
   ["Valid launcher-generated bindings still complete fully fake initialization with the existing model shapes, target and one mocked warm."
    "For every missing/malformed/extra-key/oversized source or process binding, assert rejection before fake Core, asset reads, compile, warm, or listener creation. Include {}, False, wrong marker, short/nonhex digest, negative/bool counts, absent/zero/bool ticks or frequency, invalid/oversized timestamps and extra path/env-like fields."
    "Assert the resulting identity has exactly the documented source/process fields, valid bounded field values and a bounded serialized size; retain the existing frozen-record/no-reread and no-private-content tests."]}]
